# Intelli-route

Read `intelli-route/manifest.json` only to classify. Fetch a skill body only after its id is in `loads`. Stop at four.

A paste or dump with no single ask goes through `control-feeder`, then classify the Feed.

1. No map, unknowns dominate, authorization is the unknown, or a multi-session effort whose route is still fog → route `empty` (`eva-emptiness`). The body is `eva-emptiness/skills/eva-emptiness/SKILL.md` in this plugins repo.
2. Multi-step, until-done, or the same step is being redone → route `card` (`control-graph`) with a budget and one verify command.
3. Otherwise → route `light` (`pstack-map`, then one pstack playbook or the house row).

Add a signal skill only when its `when` matches. A machine choice (quantum, QPU, GPU placement, Hamiltonian, entanglement, LEO handover, beam switching, obstruction, conjunction screen, Stargaze, space situational awareness, NISQ, BQP, or a closed decision software will branch on) loads `split-machine` and stops if its confidence is low. Shipping, review load, a repeated bad pattern, fan-out, or a session lookback loads `trust-stack`. That skill does not merge. A builder brief, a steering-doc edit, or an alignment interview that must end in an invariant card loads `steer-log`. A long stretch, a break, a context switch, or a resume that stays on this harness and directory loads `steer-accel`. When a settled conversation needs a spec before code, load `craft`. A goal that is a closed decision that must be corroborated loads `concordance`. That skill emits its own card. This rule does not compare the labels. A master plan loads `master-planner`. A hard-to-revert choice loads `higher-order-decision-architect`. A roadmap or blueprint cards load `stellar-spacemap`. Cross-file design, a glossary, or a domain model loads `architecture-synthesis`. Load one of that family, not all four. That set includes `odysseus-navigator` for a plan, architecture, or review. Blocking tickets, once a destination is named, load `mission-map`, and each builder card still goes through `steer-log`. A resume that changes harness or directory loads `pulse-memory`. A task graph of tickets loads `git-worktrees`. An alignment name loads `aihero-map`. Do not fetch the upstream body. `clt-dual-load` is a host rule. Do not paste it and do not count it.

Pause before secrets, production, irreversible git, CV promote, unknown authorization, and money, legal, or health acts. On that pause, emit the route and stop.

Emit situation, route, loads, skips, playbook, hitl, and next. Then do that next step. Credit Lauren Tan / pstack MIT when a playbook runs. Do not rewrite `pstack-models.mdc`. Do not copy skill bodies into this repo.
